WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
Solar is booming.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:09.190
In 2024, solar panels worldwide
generated 2,143 terawatt hours.

3
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:15.730
In 2025, 2,779: about 30 per cent more.

4
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:22.470
Since 2000, coal's share of world electricity
has fallen from 38 to 33.1 per cent.

5
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.970
Yet the world used more
fossil fuel than ever.

6
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.930
Oil: 103 million barrels a day.

7
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.390
How can both be true?

8
00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.990
Are the solar figures wrong?

9
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.830
Was the fuel stockpiled?

10
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.150
In this mission, you'll compare the
electricity mix of 2000 and 2025,

11
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.950
and map where coal is burned.

12
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.790
Then you'll see who uses
the most energy per person,

13
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:51.850
and who has no electricity at
all: 655 million people in 2024.

14
00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:57.160
Your mission: explain how solar can boom
while fossil fuel use breaks records.
